ment Study (OHTS).</article-title><source>Ophthalmology</source><volume>108</volume><fpage>1779</fpage><lpage>1788</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11581049</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002510-Szijarto1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Szijarto</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Schvoller</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Poto</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuhn</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kovacs</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Pseudophakic retinal detachment after phacoemulsification.</article-title><source>Ann Ophthalmol (Skokie)</source><volume>39</volume><fpage>134</fpage><lpage>139</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17984502</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002510-SchmitzValckenberg1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmitz-Valckenberg</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bindewald-Wittich</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dolar-Szczasny</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dreyhaupt</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolf</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Correlation between the area of increased autofluorescence surrounding geographic atrophy and disease progression in patients with AMD.</article-title><source>Invest Ophthalmol Vis Sci</source><volume>47</volume><fpage>2648</fpage><lpage>2654</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16723482</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002510-Hyman1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hyman</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name><name><surname>Lilienfeld</surnam